# CapstoneMergeBaseOffset, mergeGlobalBaseUses: several PseudoCapGlobalBase of
# one constant-pool address (the shape MachineCSE's PRE leaves behind when it
# hoists the auipc + addi to a common dominator but not the base, whose operand
# is a virtual register) become one base.
#
# The primary is chosen by INSTRUCTION order, never by use-list order. The
# use list of a register lists its operands in the order they were (re)added,
# which is instruction order after parsing and arbitrary after a pass has
# rewritten an operand. @same_block_reversed constructs the adverse order:
# machine-cse runs first and copy-propagates %2 = COPY %1 into the FIRST base,
# re-adding that operand at the END of %1's use list, behind the second base's;
# the second base carries an extra implicit use so that machine-cse does not
# merge the two itself (it would, otherwise), and they reach the merge pass as
# a same-block pair with the use list reversed (the same extra use keeps
# machine-cse and its PRE from merging the pairs of the other cases, so that
# every case reaches the merge pass). Choosing by use-list order
# picks the LATER base, leaves it in place, and rewrites the earlier load to a
# register that is defined after it (the verifier then fails with a
# use-before-def); choosing by block order keeps the earlier base. Control on
# the superseded lane's llc (use-list order): `FLD %5, 0` printed BEFORE
# `%5 = PseudoCapGlobalBase`, and @child_block_gp_def merged across the gp
# write; this file's CHECKs reject both.
#
# The derivation must keep the same authority and lifetime: when anything in
# the function writes gp, the two bases may derive from different gp values
# and are not merged (@child_block_gp_def; @child_block_merged is the same shape
# without the write, merged into the dominating base, which stays in place).
# @sibling_blocks is 544.nab_r mme34's shape: no base in Lo's block, so the
# first one in function order is moved to just after Lo, where it dominates
# the other's uses; after the merge the capability's uses are loads at two
# offsets, so the %pcrel_lo fold does not apply and the addi stays.
#
#
# A merged base keeps Lo's COMPLETE address, as every pool base does: there is
# no %pcrel_lo fold (deleting Lo, deriving from the auipc's high part, pushing
# the low part into the loads). @sibling_equal_offsets and @policy_boundary are
# the shapes such a fold would take after a merge (every load at one common
# offset): with H = 2^38, gp bounds [H-4096, H), the auipc at H-4096 and the
# entry at H-16, the relocation is hi +4096 / lo -16; scc of the complete
# address forms H-16 (tagged), scc of the high part forms H, refused under
# sv39 and written untagged, and the `fld -16` off it faults at the unchanged
# effective address. These CHECKs keep the addi. @single_use is the same
# boundary with one base and one load: it keeps the addi too.
#
# RUN: llc -mtriple=capstone64 -mattr=+m,+f,+d -capstone-gp-free -capstone-image-gp -run-pass=machine-cse,capstone-merge-base-offset -verify-machineinstrs -o - %s | FileCheck %s
--- |
  target triple = "capstone64"
  define void @same_block_reversed() { ret void }
  define void @sibling_blocks() { ret void }
  define void @child_block_gp_def() { ret void }
  define void @child_block_merged() { ret void }
  define void @sibling_equal_offsets() { ret void }
  define void @policy_boundary() { ret void }
  define void @single_use() { ret void }
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: same_block_reversed
# CHECK:       [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI {{%[0-9]+}}, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi0>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 8
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
name: same_block_reversed
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x5
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi0>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi0>
    %2:gpr = COPY %1
    %3:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %2, implicit $x3
    %4:fpr64 = FLD %3, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    %5:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3, implicit $x5
    %6:fpr64 = FLD %5, 8 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    %7:fpr64 = nofpexcept FADD_D %4, %6, 7, implicit $frm
    $f10_d = COPY %7
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: sibling_blocks
# CHECK:       [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI {{%[0-9]+}}, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi1>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  BNE {{%[0-9]+}}, $x0, %bb.2
# CHECK:       bb.1:
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
# CHECK:       {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK:       bb.2:
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
# CHECK:       {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 8
name: sibling_blocks
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x10, $x5
    successors: %bb.1, %bb.2
    %2:gpr = COPY $x10
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi1>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi1>
    BNE %2, $x0, %bb.2
    PseudoBR %bb.1

  bb.1:
    %4:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %5:fpr64 = FLD %4, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    $f10_d = COPY %5
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d

  bb.2:
    liveins: $x5
    %6:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3, implicit $x5
    %7:fpr64 = FLD %6, 8 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    $f10_d = COPY %7
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: child_block_gp_def
# CHECK:       [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI {{%[0-9]+}}, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi2>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK:       bb.1:
# CHECK:       $x3 = COPY
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP2:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP2]], 8
name: child_block_gp_def
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x10
    successors: %bb.1
    %2:gpr = COPY $x10
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi2>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi2>
    %3:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %4:fpr64 = FLD %3, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    PseudoBR %bb.1

  bb.1:
    $x3 = COPY %2
    %6:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %7:fpr64 = FLD %6, 8 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    %8:fpr64 = nofpexcept FADD_D %4, %7, 7, implicit $frm
    $f10_d = COPY %8
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: child_block_merged
# CHECK:       [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI {{%[0-9]+}}, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi3>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK:       bb.1:
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
# CHECK:       {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 8
name: child_block_merged
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x10, $x5
    successors: %bb.1
    %2:gpr = COPY $x10
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi3>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi3>
    %3:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %4:fpr64 = FLD %3, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    PseudoBR %bb.1

  bb.1:
    liveins: $x5
    %6:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3, implicit $x5
    %7:fpr64 = FLD %6, 8 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    %8:fpr64 = nofpexcept FADD_D %4, %7, 7, implicit $frm
    $f10_d = COPY %8
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: sibling_equal_offsets
# CHECK:       [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI {{%[0-9]+}}, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi4>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  BNE {{%[0-9]+}}, $x0, %bb.2
# CHECK:       bb.1:
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
# CHECK:       {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK:       bb.2:
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
# CHECK:       {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
name: sibling_equal_offsets
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x10, $x5
    successors: %bb.1, %bb.2
    %2:gpr = COPY $x10
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi4>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi4>
    BNE %2, $x0, %bb.2
    PseudoBR %bb.1

  bb.1:
    %4:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %5:fpr64 = FLD %4, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    $f10_d = COPY %5
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d

  bb.2:
    liveins: $x5
    %6:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3, implicit $x5
    %7:fpr64 = FLD %6, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    $f10_d = COPY %7
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: policy_boundary
# CHECK:       [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI {{%[0-9]+}}, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi5>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
# CHECK-NOT:   PseudoCapGlobalBase
name: policy_boundary
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x5
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi5>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi5>
    %3:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %4:fpr64 = FLD %3, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    %5:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3, implicit $x5
    %6:fpr64 = FLD %5, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    %7:fpr64 = nofpexcept FADD_D %4, %6, 7, implicit $frm
    $f10_d = COPY %7
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
---
# CHECK-LABEL: name: single_use
# CHECK:       [[HI:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[LO:%[0-9]+]]:gpr = ADDI [[HI]], target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi6>
# CHECK-NEXT:  [[CAP:%[0-9]+]]:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase [[LO]], implicit $x3
# CHECK-NEXT:  {{%[0-9]+}}:fpr64 = FLD [[CAP]], 0
name: single_use
tracksRegLiveness: true
constants:
  - id: 0
    value: 'double 1.000000e+00'
    alignment: 8
body: |
  bb.0:
    %0:gpr = AUIPC target-flags(capstone-pcrel-hi) %const.0, pre-instr-symbol <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi6>
    %1:gpr = ADDI %0, target-flags(capstone-pcrel-lo) <mcsymbol .Lpcrel_hi6>
    %3:gpcr = PseudoCapGlobalBase %1, implicit $x3
    %4:fpr64 = FLD %3, 0 :: (load (s64) from constant-pool, addrspace 200)
    $f10_d = COPY %4
    PseudoRET implicit $f10_d
...
